    "narrative": "Our strongest plays today center around **Taylor Ward** (67.54) and **Matt Chapman** (66.91), who both benefit from favorable park environments and manageable matchups against mid-rotation arms. **Taylor Ward** is our clear headliner; leading off against Canning provides a critical volume boost (+10% order adjustment), and the park factor (+16%) elevates his power-speed profile. Similarly, **Matt Chapman** is in a prime spot against Javier Assad, capitalizing on a strong platoon advantage (+7%) and a top-of-the-order assignment (+6%) that should yield high-leverage counting stats. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start despite the tough matchup against Jack Flaherty (3.92 xERA); his elite floor and lineup placement ensure he remains our primary engine for RBI and run production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Bryson Stott** (48.37), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Bryson Stott** benefits from a positive platoon split against Jacob Misiorowski, the optimizer penalized him heavily for facing a pitcher with a 2.79 xERA, indicating that despite his utility, he is currently better suited for the bench than displacing our higher-ceiling options like **Gavin Sheets** (63.36) or **Geraldo Perdomo** (62.54). **Geraldo Perdomo** warrants specific attention for his high floor today\u2014despite the inherent risk of a lefty-on-lefty matchup against Nick Lodolo, his recent efficiency and park-adjusted projection (+3%) make him a superior play to our alternatives. \n\nLooking at the margins, we are closely monitoring the lineups for **Jonathan Aranda** (56.48) and **Gleyber Torres** (49.75), as both are currently operating on \"Lineup Pending\" status with fairly middling projections. **Jonathan Aranda** faces a significant test against Sam Aldegheri; while the 5.47 xERA is inviting, his platoon disadvantage (-12%) caps his upside. Meanwhile, we continue to manage the health of our depth, with **Will Smith** and **Cal Raleigh** remaining sidelined on the IL. We are proceeding with caution, specifically keeping an eye on **Drew Gilbert** (48.98), who draws a favorable matchup but is relegated to the nine-hole, significantly dampening his run-scoring probability.",
